# hal-voice -- where to restore HAL's voice clips from.
#
# Copy this file to  voice-source.local  (that name is git-ignored) and put a
# single source on one uncommented line. fetch-voice-lines.py reads the first
# non-comment line. You can also set $HALVOICE_VOICE_SOURCE or pass --source.
#
# A source can be any ONE of:
#   - a local folder of HAL *.mp3 clips        /home/you/hal-clips
#   - a local archive of them                  /home/you/hal-clips.tar.gz
#   - an http(s) URL to such an archive        https://my-private-bucket/hal-clips.tar.gz
#   - an rsync target                          you@host:/srv/hal-clips/
#
# Use only audio you legally own / have the right to use. Keep it local; do not
# redistribute the clips or any voice model trained from them.

# /home/you/hal-clips
